# The code-signing identity this project is built with, as a SHA-1 hash.
#
# Why pinned: this Mac carries two "Developer ID Application" certificates, and `bundle.sh` picks
# the first it finds. macOS keys the Accessibility grant to the signature's designated requirement,
# so building with the other one silently produces an app that is *not* the app TCC trusts — a
# ticked checkbox and an `AXIsProcessTrusted()` that returns false, with no error to explain it.
# Naming the hash makes the build reproducible regardless of certificate order or renewals.
#
# Not a secret: a certificate fingerprint is public, and signing needs the private key in the
# keychain, which this file does not contain.
#
# To change it: `security find-identity -p codesigning` and put the hash below, or override for one
# build with `SPACIAL_SIGN_IDENTITY=<hash> Scripts/bundle.sh`. On a machine without this
# certificate, delete the line (or the file) and bundle.sh falls back to its usual search order.
<sign-identity SHA-1>
